{'symbol': 'INCY', 'date': '2019-10-11 22:30:00', 'title': 'INCYTE ANNOUNCES POSITIVE 52-WEEK RESULTS FROM RANDOMIZED PHASE 2 STUDY OF RUXOLITINIB CREAM IN PATIENTS WITH VITILIGO', 'text': 'INCYTE ANNOUNCED POSITIVE 52-WEEK RESULTS FROM ITS RANDOMIZED, DOUBLE-BLIND, DOSE-RANGING, PHASE 2 STUDY EVALUATING RUXOLITINIB CREAM, A NONSTEROIDAL, ANTI-INFLAMMATORY, JAK INHIBITOR THERAPY, IN ADULT PATIENTS WITH VITILIGO. AS PREVIOUSLY ANNOUNCED, THE STUDY MET ITS PRIMARY ENDPOINT, DEMONSTRATING THAT SIGNIFICANTLY MORE PATIENTS TREATED WITH RUXOLITINIB CREAM FOR 24 WEEKS ACHIEVED A =50% IMPROVEMENT FROM BASELINE IN THE FACIAL VITILIGO AREA SEVERITY INDEX (F-VASI50) SCORE COMPARED TO PATIENTS TREATED WITH A VEHICLE CONTROL (NON-MEDICATED CREAM). UPDATED RESULTS AT WEEK 52 SHOW SUBSTANTIAL IMPROVEMENTS IN TOTAL BODY REPIGMENTATION WITH RUXOLITINIB CREAM, MEASURED BY THE PROPORTION OF PATIENTS ACHIEVING A =50% IMPROVEMENT FROM BASELINE IN THE TOTAL VITILIGO AREA SEVERITY INDEX (T-VASI50), A KEY SECONDARY ENDPOINT. IN ADDITION, AFTER 52 WEEKS OF TREATMENT WITH RUXOLITINIB CREAM 1.5% ADMINISTERED TWICE DAILY (BID), 58% OF PATIENTS ACHIEVED F-VASI50 AND 51% OF PATIENTS ACHIEVED A =75% IMPROVEMENT (F-VASI75). F-VASI75 AFTER 24 WEEKS IS THE PRIMARY OUTCOME MEASURE OF BOTH THE TRUE-V1 AND TRUE-V2 RANDOMIZED PHASE 3 TRIALS THAT ARE ALREADY UNDERWAY. KEY 52-WEEK RESULTS INCLUDE: A LONGER DURATION OF THERAPY, FROM WEEK 24 TO WEEK 52, WAS ASSOCIATED WITH GREATER REPIGMENTATION, AS OBJECTIVELY ASSESSED USING THE VASI. THE PERCENTAGE OF PATIENTS RECEIVING 1.5% RUXOLITINIB CREAM BID WHO ACHIEVED F-VASI50 INCREASED FROM WEEK 24 TO WEEK 52 (45.5% TO 57.6%, RESPECTIVELY). A =75% (F-VASI75) AND =90% (F-VASI90) IMPROVEMENT FROM BASELINE IN F-VASI SCORE WAS ACHIEVED BY 51.5% AND 33.3% OF PATIENTS TREATED WITH 1.5% RUXOLITINIB CREAM BID AT 52 WEEKS, COMPARED TO 30% AND 12% OF PATIENTS AT 24 WEEKS, RESPECTIVELY. AMONG ALL PATIENTS TREATED WITH 1.5% RUXOLITINIB CREAM BID, THE PROPORTION OF PATIENTS ACHIEVING T-VASI50 AT WEEK 52 WAS 36.4%. AMONG PATIENTS WITH A BASELINE TOTAL BODY SURFACE AREA OF <20% (THE BODY SURFACE AREA LIMITED FOR TREATMENT), 45.0% RECEIVING THE 1.5% BID DOSE ACHIEVED A T-VASI50 RESPONSE AT 52 WEEKS. THE PROPORTION OF PATIENTS RECEIVING RUXOLITINIB CREAM 1.5% BID WHO ACHIEVED FACIAL PHYSICIAN GLOBAL VITILIGO ASSESSMENT (F-PHGVA) SCORES OF CLEAR (NO SIGNS OF VITILIGO) OR ALMOST CLEAR (ONLY SPECKS OF DEPIGMENTATION PRESENT) SKIN INCREASED FROM WEEK 24 TO WEEK 52 (9.1% AND 21.2%, RESPECTIVELY). RUXOLITINIB CREAM WAS GENERALLY WELL-TOLERATED AT ALL DOSAGE STRENGTHS AND NO TREATMENT-RELATED SERIOUS ADVERSE EVENTS WERE REPORTED.'}{'symbol': 'INCY', 'date': '2019-10-11 22:30:00', 'title': 'INCYTE ANNOUNCES POSITIVE 52-WEEK RESULTS FROM RANDOMIZED PHASE 2 STUDY OF RUXOLITINIB CREAM IN PATIENTS WITH VITILIGO', 'text': 'INCYTE ANNOUNCED POSITIVE 52-WEEK RESULTS FROM ITS RANDOMIZED, DOUBLE-BLIND, DOSE-RANGING, PHASE 2 STUDY EVALUATING RUXOLITINIB CREAM, A NONSTEROIDAL, ANTI-INFLAMMATORY, JAK INHIBITOR THERAPY, IN ADULT PATIENTS WITH VITILIGO. AS PREVIOUSLY ANNOUNCED, THE STUDY MET ITS PRIMARY ENDPOINT, DEMONSTRATING THAT SIGNIFICANTLY MORE PATIENTS TREATED WITH RUXOLITINIB CREAM FOR 24 WEEKS ACHIEVED A =50% IMPROVEMENT FROM BASELINE IN THE FACIAL VITILIGO AREA SEVERITY INDEX (F-VASI50) SCORE COMPARED TO PATIENTS TREATED WITH A VEHICLE CONTROL (NON-MEDICATED CREAM). UPDATED RESULTS AT WEEK 52 SHOW SUBSTANTIAL IMPROVEMENTS IN TOTAL BODY REPIGMENTATION WITH RUXOLITINIB CREAM, MEASURED BY THE PROPORTION OF PATIENTS ACHIEVING A =50% IMPROVEMENT FROM BASELINE IN THE TOTAL VITILIGO AREA SEVERITY INDEX (T-VASI50), A KEY SECONDARY ENDPOINT. IN ADDITION, AFTER 52 WEEKS OF TREATMENT WITH RUXOLITINIB CREAM 1.5% ADMINISTERED TWICE DAILY (BID), 58% OF PATIENTS ACHIEVED F-VASI50 AND 51% OF PATIENTS ACHIEVED A =75% IMPROVEMENT (F-VASI75). F-VASI75 AFTER 24 WEEKS IS THE PRIMARY OUTCOME MEASURE OF BOTH THE TRUE-V1 AND TRUE-V2 RANDOMIZED PHASE 3 TRIALS THAT ARE ALREADY 